{"baseRefName":"master","body":"## Problem\n\nThe `:notify` handler was calling `send_long_message` directly on forum channels (type 15) when neither `forum_title` nor `forum_reply_to_latest` was set. Discord rejects direct messages to forum channels — they require creating a post/thread.\n\nThis caused GLaDOS's 8am morning message cron to silently fail delivery since ~July 6 (28 undelivered messages piled up in `tmp/notify/draft/`). Sheogorath's board report was unaffected because it uses `forum_reply_to_latest: true`.\n\n## Fix\n\n- When `forum_title` is present, append a date suffix for unique daily thread names (e.g. \"GLaDOS Morning Brief — Aug 12, 2026\")\n- Add fallback branch: if targeting a forum channel without explicit forum settings, auto-create a forum post with `{agent_name} — {date}` as the title\n- Non-forum channels are unaffected (still hit the `send_long_message` path)\n\n## Also Applied (outside this repo)\n\n- Set `forum_title: \"GLaDOS Morning Brief\"` in `~/.brainiac/cron.json` for the morning message job\n\n## Version\n\n0.0.10 → 0.0.11","headRefName":"glados/fix-forum-channel-notify-handler","title":"Fix notify handler silently failing on forum channels"}
